From d60614a59c1e2eec9d1cc5fa962800d6c6afd9b6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 02:01:14 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 09/18] metrics: chain tip, initial block download and block
 connect time

The tip's height and block timestamp live under cs_main; they are
mirrored into gauges where the tip changes (Chainstate::UpdateTip, for
the active chainstate) and once at startup, with the lock already held,
so scraping reads atomics only. The tip's age is computed when scraped
(and is negative while the tip's timestamp is ahead of the clock, as
with quickly mined regtest blocks). Initial block download is 1 until
the existing IBD latch flips.

ConnectBlock's duration goes to a histogram through the validating
thread's event ring: one extra clock read, only when metrics are on.
